WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.656 --> 00:00:14.463
The after the funeral Aunt Polly's kisses stopped.

2
00:00:15.264 --> 00:00:16.704
At breakfast she was angry.

3
00:00:16.724 --> 00:00:21.807
"Tom Sawyer, I cannot believe you were so hard-hearted.

4
00:00:22.628 --> 00:00:25.710
You made me, and everyone else, suffer for almost a week.

5
00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:29.352
You paddled on a log to come to your funeral.

6
00:00:30.252 --> 00:00:32.694
You could have at least come home and let me know that you weren't dead."

7
00:00:33.775 --> 00:00:34.655
Tom looked away.

8
00:00:35.456 --> 00:00:39.859
He knew that his aunt had suffered because of him, and his conscience wouldn't allow him to forget

9
00:00:39.919 --> 00:00:43.802
it. "You should have let me know," continued Aunt Polly.

10
00:00:44.682 --> 00:00:47.084
Tom was sure that his guilty conscience was showing.

11
00:00:47.104 --> 00:00:53.108
"Tell me, Tom, that you would have come if you had thought of it."

12
00:00:53.128 --> 00:00:58.132
"I ah well I don't know," stammered Tom.

13
00:00:58.676 --> 00:01:00.337
"It would have spoiled everything."

14
00:01:00.357 --> 00:01:04.259
"Oh, Tom, you break my heart," said Aunt Polly.

15
00:01:04.279 --> 00:01:07.221
"If you loved me, you would have come home.

16
00:01:07.941 --> 00:01:10.382
But all you care about are your ruined plans."

17
00:01:11.583 --> 00:01:13.724
Tom's conscience was paining him greatly.

18
00:01:13.744 --> 00:01:17.466
"You know, Auntie, I care for you."

19
00:01:17.486 --> 00:01:23.049
"I'd know better if you acted more like it," answered his aunt in a hurt tone.

20
00:01:23.069 --> 00:01:25.951
"I did wrong," confessed Tom.

21
00:01:25.971 --> 00:01:27.632
"I should have thought of you.

22
00:01:28.568 --> 00:01:30.789
In any case I did dream of you."

23
00:01:30.809 --> 00:01:34.571
"That isn't much," said Aunt Polly sadly.

24
00:01:34.591 --> 00:01:36.451
"But what did you dream about?"

25
00:01:36.471 --> 00:01:41.593
"It was Wednesday night, and I dreamed that you and Joe's mother were sitting here."

26
00:01:41.613 --> 00:01:43.754
"Why, she was here!"

27
00:01:44.195 --> 00:01:45.215
exclaimed Aunt Polly.

28
00:01:45.235 --> 00:01:47.196
"What else did you dream about?"

29
00:01:47.216 --> 00:01:51.117
"Oh, lots of stuff," said Tom.

30
00:01:51.137 --> 00:01:54.019
"But it's all kind of hazy."

31
00:01:54.039 --> 00:01:57.160
"Do try to remember," urged Aunt Polly.

32
00:01:58.824 --> 00:02:04.747
"Well, there was the wind, it blew "Yes," said Aunt Polly excitedly.

33
00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.787
"The wind did blow something.

34
00:02:07.508 --> 00:02:08.228
What did it blow?"

35
00:02:09.008 --> 00:02:13.330
Tom pressed his fingers to his forehead and said, "It blew the candle."

36
00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:16.852
"Mercy!" exclaimed Aunt Polly.

37
00:02:16.872 --> 00:02:17.952
"That's right.

38
00:02:18.593 --> 00:02:19.093
Go on."

39
00:02:19.113 --> 00:02:22.654
"It's all coming back to me now," cried Tom.

40
00:02:22.674 --> 00:02:26.396
"You said I wasn't bad, and then you started to cry."

41
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.881
"I did," said Aunt Polly.

42
00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:34.102
"Sereny Harper is going to hear about this before I'm an hour older.

43
00:02:34.642 --> 00:02:35.082
Go on."

44
00:02:35.102 --> 00:02:41.984
"Then Joe's mother started crying," Tom continued, "and she said Joe wasn't bad either.

45
00:02:42.704 --> 00:02:47.005
She also wished she hadn't punished Joe for taking the cream when she was the one who had

46
00:02:47.045 --> 00:02:47.806
thrown it out."

47
00:02:49.106 --> 00:02:54.127
"Tom," cried Aunt Polly, "you were dreaming like a prophet."

48
00:02:55.168 --> 00:02:56.648
Tom told his aunt everything.

49
00:02:57.416 --> 00:03:00.078
He didn't leave out a thing, and Aunt Polly was in awe.

50
00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:04.582
Finally Tom said, "I think you prayed for me.

51
00:03:05.303 --> 00:03:06.124
I was sorry.

52
00:03:06.784 --> 00:03:08.906
So I wrote a note saying we weren't dead.

53
00:03:09.547 --> 00:03:12.069
I put it on your table, and then I kissed you."

54
00:03:12.089 --> 00:03:18.574
"I know it's only a dream, but I can forgive you now," said Aunt Polly, hugging Tom.

55
00:03:20.276 --> 00:03:24.740
Sid thought the dream sounded too perfect to be a dream, but he kept his opinion to himself.

56
00:03:25.844 --> 00:03:29.226
When Tom was at school, Aunt Polly went to tell Joe's mother about the dream.

57
00:03:30.907 --> 00:03:33.689
At lunch Tom came home to a very angry aunt.

58
00:03:34.869 --> 00:03:37.451
"I should skin you alive," she said.

59
00:03:37.471 --> 00:03:40.553
"I ran over to Sereny Harper like an old fool.

60
00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:43.774
I told her about your amazing dream.

61
00:03:44.555 --> 00:03:48.097
She told me that Joe had told her you were here that night.

62
00:03:49.038 --> 00:03:50.218
It wasn't a dream at all!"

63
00:03:51.079 --> 00:03:52.980
Tom truly felt sorry for his joke.

64
00:03:53.692 --> 00:03:57.813
It had seemed like a good idea at breakfast, but now it just seemed mean.

65
00:03:57.833 --> 00:04:01.694
"You let me make a fool of myself.

66
00:04:02.455 --> 00:04:03.855
What kind of boy are you?"

67
00:04:04.295 --> 00:04:05.155
asked Aunt Polly.

68
00:04:05.816 --> 00:04:07.296
Tom hung his head in shame.

69
00:04:07.316 --> 00:04:09.737
"Why did you come over that night?

70
00:04:10.437 --> 00:04:12.137
Did you come to laugh at our troubles?"

71
00:04:12.577 --> 00:04:13.218
she demanded.

72
00:04:13.238 --> 00:04:16.519
"No," said Tom.

73
00:04:16.539 --> 00:04:18.719
"I came to tell you not to worry.

74
00:04:19.339 --> 00:04:21.320
I even wrote a note on a piece of bark.

75
00:04:22.016 --> 00:04:26.157
When I got the idea about the funeral, I put the note back in my pocket.

76
00:04:26.638 --> 00:04:28.178
But I did kiss you good-night."

77
00:04:28.938 --> 00:04:31.119
The hard lines on his aunt's face melted.

78
00:04:31.839 --> 00:04:35.340
The emotion in Tom's voice sounded too real for this to be a lie.

79
00:04:37.521 --> 00:04:41.542
After Tom returned to school, Aunt Polly wanted to see if she could find the piece of bark.

80
00:04:42.563 --> 00:04:46.304
She wondered if Tom really did write a note, or if this was just another one of his

81
00:04:46.344 --> 00:04:52.179
stories. Aunt Polly couldn't decide what to do, so she stood for several minutes, debating with herself.

82
00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.221
Curiosity finally got the better of her.

83
00:04:57.222 --> 00:04:59.163
She went into Tom's room and looked around.

84
00:05:00.303 --> 00:05:03.966
Lying on the floor was the piece of bark, and on the back was Tom's note.

85
00:05:05.006 --> 00:05:07.468
As Aunt Polly read it, tears came to her eyes.

86
00:05:07.488 --> 00:05:14.632
"Now I can forgive Tom, even though he has committed a million sins," she murmured.
